      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IDEAL ANDY (2) came from wider when runner-up two runs back at Goulburn before another sound effort at his latest appearance at Canberra, beaten 1.4 metres into third after racing parked but sticking on. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Big chance. ROYAL VILLA (7) hit her peak and scored last week at Goulburn, getting home by 2.6 metres. Should enjoy a nice smother from this draw and will be looking for a split at some stage. If she gets it she is good enough to win a race of this calibre. MACHX THE STRANGER (3) draws well and must be considered after she finished third at Wagga a week-and-a-half ago. WARRAWEE CRUZIN (1) has been coming from wider or second row barriers of late so is much better served by the ace draw and owns a good record at this circuit and distance.",
